Z||000000||80's BOY||12-26-2000||06:24 PM||||the ones i tried from the mustang were brown.<BR>they were supposed to be 19#.<BR>others i have seen have been pink.<BR>what are those?? do the top colors mean something??<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||12-26-2000||08:38 PM||||I would be learly about just tring any old Ford injector.  The 5.0 injectors are high impedence injectors, and some other Fords (like the turbo 2.3 like the old SVO's and turbo Tbird's) use low impedence injectors.  Mixing each of them will burn up your computer.  <P>Just a warning....<P>BTW, I have no idea what pink injectors are, the brown's are 19's (Motorsport injectors are: brown=19, light blue=24, red=30, dark blue=36, green=42). I've had them all but the 42's....<BR>BTW again, you can mod the injectors to flow bigger numbers, I have a set of 47.7lb injectors that were moded red top 30lb inj waiting to go in the stang, they flowed within 0.5% of each other.  So you really have to know the injector you are getting (the dark blue 36lb inj can be modded to flow 77lb and idle like a kitten with a custom tuned chip!).<BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A><p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 12-26-2000).]||||reg||1
